title: CyberStrikeAI Implant - Masqueraded Beacon Scheduled From Temp or ProgramData
id: 7d4c1e0a-9b52-4f6d-8e3b-2a5f9c6b41d8
status: experimental
description: Detects the CyberStrikeAI implant binaries reported by Kaspersky (November 2026) running from staging directories. Operators persisted the conventional C2 beacon through a scheduled task named SystemUpdate that launches masqueraded binaries such as svchosts.exe or svcmon32.exe out of C:\Windows\Temp or C:\ProgramData; all LLM orchestration stays server-side, so these host artifacts are the huntable residue.
references:
  - https://securelist.com/tr/cyberstrikeai-attacks/121715/
  - https://gbhackers.com/cyberstrikeai-framework/
  - https://www.team-cymru.com/post/tracking-cyberstrikeai-usage
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-11-04
tags:
  - attack.t1190
  - attack.t1053
  - attack.t1059
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_binary:
    Image|endswith:
      - '\svchosts.exe'
      - '\svcmon32.exe'
  selection_staging_path:
    Image|contains:
      - '\Windows\Temp\'
      - '\ProgramData\'
  condition: selection_binary and selection_staging_path
falsepositives:
  - Unlikely - svchosts.exe and svcmon32.exe are deliberate near-miss names for svchost.exe and no legitimate software ships them
level: high
